5,1,1,talk,Minato,,"Hello everyone. I want to make sure we don't make the staff too tired. I'm curious about how much work people are already doing. I'll look into ""Time lost to copying existing records"" and ""Staffing of the coordination group.""","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree that staff wellbeing is important. For my part, I want to ensure we aren't overlooking external dependencies. I'll look into ""Network coverage at customer plants"" and ""In-house developer availability.""","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,"I believe we must be prudent about the financial side. I will look into ""Capital budget and software allowance"" and ""Vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work"" to ensure we can actually afford the long-term commitments.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,"I'll take a different angle! I want to see if we're actually learning from our mistakes. I'm choosing ""Outcomes of the last three internal rollouts"" and ""Record of cross-unit standardization efforts."" Let's see if we're just repeating history!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,"It's nice to meet you all. I agree with Minato that we should consider the staff's burden. I'll look into ""Misrouted deliveries in the incident logs"" and ""Handling of vendor queries"" to see where the daily friction is.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,"It sounds like we are all looking at different, important things. @George, do you think the budget will be a big problem? I hope we can find a way to help the staff without spending too much.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Budget is always a factor, but I worry more about the technical groundwork. If the infrastructure isn't ready, no amount of funding will prevent a delay. We should be careful about what we promise.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"It is not just about the initial cost, Minato. I am concerned about where the money originates and the hidden costs that appear during renewals. We must ensure the funding source is stable before committing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you're so serious! But you're right—infrastructure is key. Still, why build a fancy bridge if we don't know why the last three collapsed? I'm betting the real ""hidden cost"" is just wasting time on failed ideas.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,"I think May makes a fair point about learning from the past. However, I also hope we can look at the small, repetitive mistakes that happen every day. Those little frictions often add up to a lot of stress.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,I agree with Midori. Small things can make people very tired if they happen every day. I hope the proposals we see later will make those little frictions go away instead of adding more work.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a fair hope, Minato. However, we must also ensure that the solutions we choose don't create new, unforeseen dependencies. A simple fix on paper can become a burden if the external environment doesn't support it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,"Simplicity is often the safest path. If we choose a solution that requires constant vendor support or expensive license renewals, we are merely delaying a financial crisis. We must prioritize stability over novelty.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"Stability is boring, George! But I'll admit, it's better than a crash. I just want to make sure we aren't choosing ""simple"" just because we're too scared to fix the systemic issues that killed our previous projects.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,"I understand everyone's perspective. While systemic issues are important, I worry we might overlook the actual daily losses on the floor. Let's make sure we balance the big-picture stability with the reality of our staff's everyday effort.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we have a good plan. We are looking at money, technology, past mistakes, and the people. I hope we can find a proposal that makes everyone's day a little bit easier and happier.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. By covering these different angles, we can avoid the trap of over-promising. I look forward to seeing how our findings align to help us make a grounded and sustainable choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,"I agree. As long as we remain disciplined about the financial implications and don't let enthusiasm override our budget constraints, we should be able to reach a sensible decision. I look forward to the results.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,"I'm all set! I've got my eyes on the ghosts of projects past. Let's hope the results are actually surprising for once, otherwise, this is going to be a very short conversation! See you all in the next round.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,I'm looking forward to it too. I hope we can find a solution that truly supports the people doing the hard work every day. See you all in the next round!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
