60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A, the Workflow Assistant, sounds very helpful. It could stop people from having to write the same notes by hand and save them from that tiring copying work I found. Does it seem easy to use?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, it might save time, but I am more interested in Option D. It specifically mentions synchronization ""away from the network,"" which addresses the unstable coverage I discovered at customer plants. That is a critical detail.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, while Option D is technically thoughtful, I worry about the cost of a mobile rollout. Option C, the Supplier Data Hub, seems more stable. If it is a fixed-fee build, it avoids the licensing traps I fear.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, Option C is exactly the kind of ""grand vision"" I warned you about! A central repository for everyone to update? That's a recipe for a ghost project. It'll be abandoned in six months. Option B is much more specialized.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@George, I actually think Option C is the most promising. It directly addresses the address inconsistencies and repeated certificate requests I found. It solves a real, daily friction for our staff without being overly complex.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, if Option C helps with the address mistakes, that would be great. But @Jonathan, would Option D also help the people who are tired? I just want to make sure we don't pick something that adds more work.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, Option D helps technicians, but it requires development. Since our in-house developers are busy until Q3 and our interfaces are undocumented, we would rely entirely on external vendors. That is a risky dependency for a mobile rollout.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, that risk is precisely why I am cautious. If we rely on external vendors for a mobile app, we likely face per-head licensing that will balloon. Option C is a more contained, predictable investment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're still dreaming! Option C requires ""shared update procedures"" across business units. My research shows those cross-unit efforts almost always end without an owner. It's a death trap! Option B is a specialized tool that actually lasts.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand your concern about cross-unit efforts, but the current waste is so concrete. If we can just unify the supplier records, we stop the delivery errors and the repetitive queries immediately. It's a practical fix for a real problem.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I see. @Midori thinks Option C helps with mistakes, and @Jonathan says Option D is good for the network. But if Option C needs everyone to work together, will that make them even more tired? I'm worried.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that is a valid concern. If Option C requires constant manual updates from exhausted staff, it becomes a burden. However, Option A also requires input from multiple departments, which might lead to the same fatigue.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, you make a fair point. If Option A or C creates a perpetual administrative burden, it is not a solution. However, Option B's production costs are often hidden in recurring fees. I still lean toward C if it's a fixed-fee build.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're ignoring the evidence! Option C is a textbook example of a project that will be abandoned. Option B is a specialized resource—it's a ""narrow tool"" that provides value without demanding daily maintenance from everyone. It's the only sustainable choice here.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I hear you, but Option B doesn't solve the immediate errors on the floor. Option C targets the exact cause of our misrouted deliveries. If we prioritize the staff's daily struggle, we must fix the data.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm still a bit worried about people getting more tired. Option A sounds like it helps the most with the copying work, but if Option C stops the mistakes Midori found, maybe that's better. I'll vote for C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I cannot support Option D due to the developer shortage and undocumented interfaces. Option C is risky regarding cross-unit cooperation, but it is more grounded than A or B. I will vote for Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I have listened to the concerns. While May warns of abandonment, the immediate operational waste is too great to ignore. Provided we avoid per-head licensing and stick to a fixed-fee build, Option C is the most prudent choice. I vote for C.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,You're all walking straight into a trap! Option C is a ghost project waiting to happen. I can't in good conscience vote for a failure. I'm sticking to my guns—Option B is the only sustainable choice. I vote for B.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with the others. While I respect May's caution, we cannot ignore the daily frustration of our staff. Fixing the supplier data is the most direct way to stop those repetitive errors. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
